# Cloudflare Pages rewrites (status 200). Only paths that have no file of their own:
# a state inside a language or a page. Without these the host answers such a link with
# the root shell, which is English, so a pasted /hi/... link previewed in English.
# Paths with a shell of their own (/hi/, /hi/atlas/<page>/) are served as files.
# The targets are directories, not .../index.html: Pages drops a rule whose target ends
# in index.html as an infinite loop (it strips the name and would match again).
/en/state/*                 /en/                 200
/hi/state/*                 /hi/                 200
/en/atlas/:page/state/*     /en/atlas/:page/     200
/hi/atlas/:page/state/*     /hi/atlas/:page/     200
# The same without a language (the x-default links of a page's shell). At a domain's root
# the host would fall back to the root shell anyway; under a path of one (apps.alokm.com/
# darshan/) its fallback is that site's own root, so these have to be said. There is no
# catch-all: Pages applies a rewrite before the files, and /* would hide every one of them.
/state/*                    /                    200
/atlas/*                    /                    200
